Change (only `src/nodes.ts` + `src/commands.ts`): new `functionHolders()` at src/nodes.ts:96 walks up from a function only through *value* positions — a declaration initializer, parens/object/array literals, `as`/`satisfies`, or a wrapper call given the function as its body (so `Effect.fn("x")(function*(){…})` still counts). An inline callback inside a call chain a const holds has no written name, so `hasWrittenName`/`belongsTo` (src/nodes.ts:301) treat it as an inline body: no level added, its calls are the named function's callees.
